# Pinned to LF so a checkout produces the same working-tree bytes on every
# platform, and `cargo package` therefore produces the same archive bytes.
# This moves no stored blob: every tracked file is already LF in the object
# store, so `git add --renormalize .` is an empty commit. It changes the
# working tree at the next checkout.
#
# Release verification does not depend on this. It compares packaged entries
# against the commit's blobs, so a CRLF checkout still verifies. This stops
# the divergence arising in the first place.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary

# Defence in depth beside .gitignore and the canonical gate's tracked-vendor
# check: if a vendor document is ever force-added, keep it out of `git archive`
# and the GitHub source tarballs.
/docs/vendor/*.pdf export-ignore
